{
  "observation": "The driver now uses a continuous native outer-gutter drag with minimum fraction .12 instead of a tiny gesture that closed the actual IME. Native verification recorded actual .12 up/down drags with SDK IME true before and after both, then independently verified complete measured native focus/save rectangles. The clipped-target boundary fixture separately requires the corrected minimum fraction. Earlier forced-clipping trials are retained as diagnostic attempts; one had an accessibility timeout and another could not establish its clipping precondition. Fourteen harness boundary/integrity checks passed. Seven complete configurations and 21 complete pages plus 7 keyboard combinations from the next configuration were independently reinspected, preserving 182 native page checks and 70 complete keyboard combinations. Only uncompleted pages 08/09 and the final matrix configuration remain for actual acceptance. The checkpoint changes initialization and permitted navigation only; inverse transformation proves original independent matrix assertions unchanged. All 206 prior valid visits, product code, source planning artifacts and expected rules are unchanged. Original blocked attempts remain blocked; repair closure does not pass the case. The earlier native trial template text mentions eight combinations; its actual trial array has exactly one, and the separate continuous-drag proof is decisive.",
